    "data": {
      "key": "32CU2TBH",
      "version": 134,
      "itemType": "presentation",
      "title": "Tutorial: Introduction to FAIR4ML, a vocabulary to describe FAIR AI models",
      "creators": [
        {
          "creatorType": "presenter",
          "firstName": "Leyla Jael",
          "lastName": "Castro"
        }
      ],
      "abstractNote": "Name: Tutorial - Introduction to FAIR4ML, a vocabulary to describe FAIR AI models\n\nDescription: This tutorial provides an introduction the FAIR4ML, a schema.org extension to represent AI models (particularly ML/DL models) based on ML model cards. It first introduces metadata at a high level to then deep into FAIR4ML, including the metadata schema, its use with JSON-LD, benefits, and next steps. If finished with an early adoption of FAIR4ML. This tutorial includes hands-on exercises.\n\nKeywords: Machine learning model cards, responsible AI, transparency, documentation, metadata, schema.org, FAIR4ML, controlled vocabulary\n\nLearning objectives:\n\n\n\n\n\nExplain what ML model cards are and their purpose.\n\n\n\n\nIdentify the main sections of a model card.\n\n\n\n\nExplain why model cards are important for responsible/transparent AI\n\n\n\nPrerequisites/requirements:\n\n\n\n\n\nBasic knowledge on ML model cards \n\n\n\n\n\n\nwhat they are\n\n\n\n\nwhat their purpose is\n\n\n\n\n\nSome knowledge on semantic data\n\n\n\n\n\n\nwhat a type/class is \n\n\n\n\nwhat a property/relation is and their relation to types/classes\n\n\n\n\nhow to “read” a triple\n\n\n\n\nAdditional information:\n\n\n\nTime estimation: 30 minutes\n\n Level: Beginner / Introductory\n\n Published: 2025-09-15\n\n Latest modification: 2025-09-15\n\n License: CC-By 4.0\n\n Version: 1.0.0\n\n Identifier: DOI:10.5281/zenodo.17062369.\n\n Citation: Castro, L. J. (2025, September 15). Tutorial: Introduction to FAIR4ML, a vocabulary to describe FAIR AI models. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17062369\n\n\nOther tutorials in this series:\n\n\n\nCastro, L. J. (2025, September 15). Tutorial: Introduction to ML model cards. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17062307   \n\nCastro, L. J. (2025, September 15). Tutorial: Introduction to MLentory, a metadata registry for AI models. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17062651",
